        "userMessage": "Conversation info (untrusted metadata): ```json { \"message_id\": \"19128\", \"reply_to_id\": \"19126\", \"sender_id\": \"8518484672\", \"sender\": \"Jonathan\", \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-04-15 04:02 PDT\", \"has_reply_context\": true } ``` Sender (untrusted metadata): ```json { \"label\": \"Jonathan (8518484672)\", \"id\": \"8518484672\", \"name\": \"Jonathan\" } ``` Replied message (untrusted, for context): ```json { \"sender_label\": \"pelican\", \"body\": \"Done.\\n\\nI pushed the live sizing wider now in the runtime config.\\n\\nNew live sizing map\\n\\nIn runtime/quant-research/.trigger_config.json:\\n\\n• kelly_reference_mode: kelly_binary\\n• tier1_min_post_cost_edge: 2.5%, tier1_units: 2\\n• tier2_min_post_cost_edge: 5.0%, tier2_units: 2\\n• tier3_min_post_cost_edge: 6.5%, tier3_units: 3\\n• tier3_min_quality_score: 0.7\\n\\nThis is basically the largest safe config-only widening available inside the current tiered-units architecture.\\n\\nWhat it means on real recent live examples\\n\\nUsing live equity about $34.26k and replaying yesterday’s actually-sized trades:\\n\\n• AAPL bull_put, 6.91% edge: 1 -> 3\\n• DASH bear_call, 7.17% edge: 1 -> 3\\n• MU bull_put, 4.11% edge: stays 1\\n\\nSo yes, the strong trades get materially bigger now.\\n\\nImportant truth\\n\\nMU-like middling trades are still Kelly-clipped at 1.\\nSo if you want even those to jump to 2+, the next step is not another cosmetic tier edit. It means explicitly loosening the Kelly ceiling / broader risk behavior.\\n\\nOps truth\\n\\n• live runtime config is edited\\n• mirrored into clean harvest lane too\\n• harvest commit: 0cb18ed (config: widen live tiered sizing)\\n• no restart needed for the proof path, since sizing reads execution architecture dynamically in order_manager\\n\\nArtifact:\\n\\n• task-artifacts/PEL-094/live-sizing-widen-now-2026-04-15.md\\n\\nIf you want, next I’ll do the second punch:\\n\\n• make MU-tier trades jump too, by loosening the Kelly ceiling deliberately instead of pretending the tier map alone did it.\" } ``` Yes broader risk!",
